<title>USA: LaserSight can sell lasers in Costa Rica.</title>
<headline>LaserSight can sell lasers in Costa Rica.</headline>
<dateline>ST. LOUIS 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>LaserSight Inc, which makes lasers used to correct vision, said Tuesday it has been granted the right by the Ministry of Health of Costa Rica to sell the company's excimer laser commercially in that country.</p>
<p>In another development, LaserSight said it appointed Howard Apple Ph.D. as LaserSight Technologies' vice president of product development and engineering. Most recently, Dr. Apple was vice president of research and development for Summit Technology Inc, a U.S. excimer laser manufacturer.</p>
<p>Shares of LaserSight were trading off 1/8 at six.</p>
<p>	 Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8787</p>
